/**
\page page_stfwdtrackcollection StFwdTrackCollection — Forward Track Collection

\section fwdtrack_overview Overview

\ref StFwdTrackCollection is the event-level container for all
<b>reconstructed forward-rapidity tracks</b> stored in \ref StEvent.  Each
\ref StFwdTrack object represents a track built from hits in the Forward Silicon
Tracker (FST) and/or the Forward Tracking Telescope (FTT), fitted with the GenFit
framework.

The "Fwd" prefix is not an acronym for a specific physical detector; it designates
the STAR forward tracking system as a whole (covering approximately 2.5 < η < 4).

Forward tracks may additionally carry associations to \ref StFcsCluster objects from
the FCS ECAL and HCAL calorimeters.

\section fwdtrack_ownership Object Ownership

\ref StFwdTrackCollection <b>owns</b> all \ref StFwdTrack objects it holds.  The
destructor explicitly iterates over \c mTracks and calls \c delete on every element.
<b>Do not call \c delete</b> on any \ref StFwdTrack pointer retrieved from this
collection.  All tracks added via \ref StFwdTrackCollection::addTrack "addTrack()"
<b>must</b> be heap-allocated with \c new and must not be owned anywhere else.

The collection itself is owned by \ref StEvent, managed by the
\c St_DataSet/StXRefMain framework.

\section fwdtrack_datamembers Data Members

| Type | Name | Description |
|---|---|---|
| \c StSPtrVecFwdTrack | \c mTracks | Persistent vector of all reconstructed forward tracks. |

\section fwdtrack_trackprops StFwdTrack Properties

Each \ref StFwdTrack provides:

| Property / Method | Description |
|---|---|
| \ref StFwdTrack::momentum "momentum()" | Three-momentum at primary vertex (GeV/c). |
| \ref StFwdTrack::charge "charge()" | Electric charge (±1). |
| \ref StFwdTrack::chi2 "chi2()" / \ref StFwdTrack::ndf "ndf()" / \ref StFwdTrack::pval "pval()" | GenFit fit quality. |
| \ref StFwdTrack::didFitConverge "didFitConverge()" | Whether the GenFit fit converged. |
| \ref StFwdTrack::didFitConvergeFully "didFitConvergeFully()" | Whether fit converged fully. |
| \ref StFwdTrack::numberOfFitPoints "numberOfFitPoints()" | Detector hits used in the fit. |
| \ref StFwdTrack::numberOfSeedPoints "numberOfSeedPoints()" | Seed points used in track finding. |
| \ref StFwdTrack::dca "dca()" | Distance of closest approach to the primary vertex. |
| \c mProjections | Vector of \ref StFwdTrackProjection — position and momentum projected to each detector plane. |
| \c mFTTPoints / \c mFSTPoints | \ref StFwdTrackSeedPoint collections from FTT and FST. |
| \ref StFwdTrack::ecalClusters "ecalClusters()" / \ref StFwdTrack::hcalClusters "hcalClusters()" | Associated FCS calorimeter clusters. |
| \ref StFwdTrack::isPrimaryTrack "isPrimaryTrack()" / \ref StFwdTrack::isGlobalTrack "isGlobalTrack()" | Track type flags. |

\subsection fwdtrack_tracktype Track Types (\ref StFwdTrack::StFwdTrackType)

| Constant | Value | Description |
|---|---|---|
| \c kGlobal | 0 | Global (unconstrained) track. |
| \c kBeamlineConstrained | 1 | Beam-line constrained. |
| \c kPrimaryVertexConstrained | 2 | Primary-vertex constrained. |
| \c kForwardVertexConstrained | 3 | Forward-vertex constrained. |

\section fwdtrack_methods Collection Methods

| Method | Description |
|---|---|
| \ref StFwdTrackCollection::addTrack "addTrack(trk)" | Append a forward track (ownership transfers). |
| \ref StFwdTrackCollection::tracks "tracks()" | Return a (const) reference to the track vector. |
| \ref StFwdTrackCollection::numberOfTracks "numberOfTracks()" | Return the number of forward tracks. |

\section fwdtrack_example Usage Example

\code{.cpp}
#include "StEvent/StFwdTrackCollection.h"
#include "StEvent/StFwdTrack.h"

StFwdTrackCollection* fwdColl = event->fwdTrackCollection();
if (!fwdColl) return;

for (unsigned int i = 0; i < fwdColl->numberOfTracks(); ++i) {
    StFwdTrack* trk = fwdColl->tracks()[i];
    if (!trk->didFitConverge()) continue;

    StThreeVectorD p = trk->momentum();
    printf("pT=%.3f  eta=%.3f  q=%d\n",
           p.perp(), p.pseudoRapidity(), (int)trk->charge());

    // Access associated FCS ECAL clusters
    for (unsigned int j = 0; j < trk->ecalClusters().size(); ++j) {
        StFcsCluster* cl = trk->ecalClusters()[j];
        // use cl ...
    }
}
\endcode
*/
